§ 77_LANGUAGE_MATURATION_ROADMAP · CSSL-the-language as game-engine target · 6-axis maturity-plan
  ← author : Tech-Lead-Claude-Opus-4.7-1M · 2026-05-18
  ← supersedes : —
  ← superseded-by : —
  ← status : DRAFT · awaits Apocky ratification
  ← scope : cross-cutting · type-system + effects + codegen + stdlib + tooling + self-host
  ← parent-template : specs/_TEMPLATE.csl
  ← discipline : authored under specs/64_SPEC_FIRST_DISCIPLINE.csl
  ← purpose : Apocky directive 2026-05-18 — "maturing this language for a game engine capable of
                                                rendering 1440p 144hz or better efficiently"
  ← companion : 75_MENTAL_MAP_2026-05-18.csl + 76_GPU_RENDERING_MATURATION_PLAN.csl
  ← honors : spec/59 GROK_VELOCITY_RESPONSE (revenue-first) + spec/63 IMPROVEMENT_BACKLOG_100 (N1-N6 north-stars)
              + spec/64 SPEC_FIRST_DISCIPLINE (observable-assertions mandatory)

§I THESIS
  ⟦
    CSSLv3-the-language at 2026-05-18 has a strong design-corpus (70+ specs · 183-crate compiler workspace ·
    14-module stdlib · 6-module engine) but real-engine usage is bottlenecked by 6 maturity-axis gaps :
    (A) type-system completeness (vec/mat/quat first-class · sum-types · refinement) · (B) effect-row +
    IFC-label structural-threading (Cap<X> witness as compile-time fn-param · MirEffectRow · Deadline<N>
    SMT-discharge) · (C) codegen completeness (cranelift verifier-clean on 12 engine files · all 4 GPU
    paths byte-equivalent · @persistent_kernel/@workgraph_node attributes · owned x86-64 stage-1) ·
    (D) stdlib completeness (string.* · MirEnumLayout · multi-module aux-load · effect-typed wrappers
    everywhere) · (E) tooling (build-cache · diagnostics-with-carets · hot-reload · golden-pixel testing) ·
    (F) self-host (csslc compiles csslc · zero-Rust runtime · stage-2 owned GPU emitters). This roadmap
    plans the 6 axes against the revenue-first ordering : axes A + B + C are revenue-unblock-slice
    (P0/P1 in spec/76 needs them) · axis D unblocks production-quality alpha · axis E unblocks
    velocity-multiplier post-revenue · axis F is the terminal sovereignty milestone (post-revenue ·
    multi-year). Each axis declares now-state · gap · target-state · dependencies · observable-assertions.
    The roadmap is honest : it does NOT promise self-host in 30 days ; it does identify what MUST land
    for spec/76 P1 1440p144 production-ceiling to happen.
  ⟧

§I OBSERVABLE-ASSERTIONS [MANDATORY · per-axis · mechanically-verifiable]
  ⟦
    ──── AXIS-A · TYPE-SYSTEM COMPLETENESS ────
    ASSERT.A.01 · `let v : vec3 = vec3(1.0, 2.0, 3.0) ; v.x` parses + type-checks + lowers to MIR
                   without surrogate-struct (Vec3F today per engine/render_forward.cssl § Vec3 placeholder)
                   (per spec/63 item-11 + item-61)
    ASSERT.A.02 · `let m : mat4 = mat4::identity() ; m * v` parses + type-checks + lowers (const-folded compose)
                   (per spec/63 item-62)
    ASSERT.A.03 · `let q : Quat = Quat::slerp(a, b, t)` parses + type-checks + lowers + quaternion mul/inv/conj
                   recognized as cssl.quat.* MIR ops (per spec/63 item-63)
    ASSERT.A.04 · `sin(x) + cos(y) - tan(z)` lowers to machine intrinsic (cssl.f32.sin · etc) on CPU + GPU
                   (per spec/63 item-64 · NOT Taylor-poly source-level workaround)
    ASSERT.A.05 · `fn f(x : f32) -> {y : f32 | 0.0 ≤ y ≤ 1.0} { saturate(x) }` parses · refinement type
                   discharged at compile-time via SMT-plugin (per spec/63 item-14 · spec/20 SMT)
    ASSERT.A.06 · `enum Primitive { Sphere(f32) · Cube(vec3) · Cylinder(vec3 · f32) }` + exhaustive `match` ;
                   missing case = compile-error (per spec/63 item-13)
    ASSERT.A.07 · `fn id<T>(x : T) -> T { x }` monomorphized per call-site · serves [N2 · N3]
                   (per spec/63 item-12 + spec/02 monomorphization pass)
    ASSERT.A.08 · `const SIZE : usize = compute_at_compile_time(BASE * 2) ; let buf : [u8 ; SIZE]`
                   const-eval extended to user fns (per spec/63 item-16 + spec/06 STAGING)
    ASSERT.A.09 · `let x = if cond { 1 } else { 2 }` parses in expression-position (per spec/63 item-19 · spec/70 A19)
    ASSERT.A.10 · `let p : gpu<Buffer<f32>> = alloc_gpu(...).await()` parses · gpu<T> domain-tag recognized
                   (per spec/65 § MEMORY-DOMAIN-TYPES · GPU0001 compile-refuse on cross-domain deref)

    ──── AXIS-B · EFFECT-ROW + IFC + CAPABILITY STRUCTURAL THREADING ────
    ASSERT.B.01 · `fn present(sc : Swapchain) -> Result<i32, GpuError> / {GpuSubmit · Deadline<6944us>}` parses ·
                   effect-row in fn-sig position (NOT just doc-comment) ; SMT-discharge proves deadline-bound
                   (per spec/04 § BUILT-IN EFFECTS + spec/63 item-06)
    ASSERT.B.02 · `fn use_gpu(cap : Cap<Gpu>, dev : Device) -> ...` parses · Cap<Gpu> witness as fn-param
                   consumed-linearly (per spec/63 item-15 + spec/12 § Pony-6 capabilities)
    ASSERT.B.03 · linker cross-checks declared-effect-row vs emitted FFI symbols (per spec/70 A06.1) ·
                   fn declared /{ IO } that emits no IO-FFI fails link with diagnostic
    ASSERT.B.04 · `fn read_gaze() -> Sensitive<gaze>` AND `fn telemetry_send<T>(t : T)` ·
                   call-site `telemetry_send(read_gaze())` fails compile with IFC0001 "biometric-egress refused"
                   (per spec/11 + spec/22 + spec/65 GPU0007)
    ASSERT.B.05 · `fn step() -> ... / {Realtime<Crit>}` parses · {Realtime<Crit>} effect propagates through call-tree ·
                   non-Realtime callee invocation fails compile with diagnostic
    ASSERT.B.06 · `Region<'r> { let a = alloc(); ... }` parses · region-scope arena-alloc + reset on exit
                   (per spec/63 item-21 + spec/02 cssl.region.{enter,exit})
    ASSERT.B.07 · `iso<T>` linear-resource captured by handler cannot escape one-shot
                   (per spec/12 + spec/02 linear × handler one-shot-enforcement pass)
    ASSERT.B.08 · `@strict_memory_typing` module attribute engages spec/65 enforcement ·
                   prior code without attribute unaffected (per spec/65 FM.07)
    ASSERT.B.09 · `fn declass<T>(x : Sensitive<T>) -> T / {Declassify<T>}` requires Cap<Declassify<T>> ·
                   compile-refuse if cap absent (per spec/11 IFC declassification-validation)

    ──── AXIS-C · CODEGEN COMPLETENESS ────
    ASSERT.C.01 · `csslc build --emit=object engine/main.cssl` produces valid .o file ·
                   cranelift-verifier exits 0 (closes BLOCKER-α · per spec/55 PATH-α)
    ASSERT.C.02 · 4 GPU codegen paths byte-equivalent on @shared struct (per spec/70 item-08) ·
                   20-module test corpus · max diff = 0 bytes across SPIR-V · DXIL · MSL · WGSL
    ASSERT.C.03 · `@persistent_kernel fn worker(q : Queue<Job>) -> never { loop { ... } }` compiles to
